## Context

The Documents page ("document-rows"; `documentsPage` in
`deliverables/jetp-observatory/app.js`) names each document by its identifier,
`<code>sen-offgrid-mini-grid-2025</code>`, where the author expects its title
("Solution Mini-Grid 2025"). Author's decision (2026-09-25): **"Titles now"**,
before the next publish. The identifier stays visible, smaller or on a second
line, since other pages and URLs use it; the search matches the title too.

The title is not served for every document: `data/<CODE>.json → sources[id]`
carries it only for the 203 of 294 documents a fact cites, and
`data/documents.json` is deliberately the retrievals table alone (ticket
0858). The ledger's `documents` table (`data/jetp/documents.csv`, the target
of the migration that retires `sources.csv`; `docs/jetp-ledger-migration.md`)
holds a title for every document. Served views stay in normal form: one file =
one table, joined at read time.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The ledger `documents` table is served as its own view, built by its own
      script so no other view's bytes or recorded input hashes move; size well
      under the pre-commit ceiling.
- [ ] Each Documents row shows the title, escaped, with the identifier as a
      second line; a document with no title falls back to the identifier.
- [ ] The search matches titles as well as identifiers and addresses.
- [ ] Render tests first; positive control: `idn-cipp-2023`, whose title is in
      no country view, shows "Comprehensive Investment and Policy Plan".
- [ ] Browser recipe green on the local preview and the public bundle, row
      height limit held; `make check-fast`, `make lint`, full `make check` on
      padme green.
